=== layout: section

# The Cell Cycle


=== layout: one-panel

# Phases of the Cell Cycle

@body

- The cell cycle consists of
- Mitotic (M) phase (mitosis and cytokinesis)
- Interphase (cell growth and copying of chromosomes in preparation for cell division)
  - Interphase is about 90% of the cell cycle


=== layout: big-image

@image

![The cell cycle: interphase and the mitotic phase.](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/cell_cycle_phases.svg)

@caption

The cell cycle: interphase and the mitotic phase.

=== layout: two-panels

# Four Stages of the Cell Cycle

@left

- Interphase has three stages\: G1, S, and G2
- Mitosis occurs after G2
- Checkpoints control transitions for G1 into S and G2 into M

@right

![Slide image 4](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/image_004.jpg)

=== layout: one-panel

# Cell-cycle checkpoints

@body

![Cell cycle with G1, G2, and M checkpoints](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/cell_cycle_checkpoints.svg)

=== layout: image-comparison

# G₁ checkpoint

@top-left

![G₁ checkpoint: stop state](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/g1_checkpoint_stop.svg)

@top-right

![G₁ checkpoint: go-ahead state](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/g1_checkpoint_go.svg)

@bottom-left

Without a go-ahead signal, the cell enters G₀.

@bottom-right

With a go-ahead signal, the cell continues the cell cycle.

=== layout: image-comparison

# M checkpoint

@top-left

![M checkpoint: stop state](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/m_checkpoint_stop.svg)

@top-right

![M checkpoint: go-ahead state](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/m_checkpoint_go.svg)

@bottom-left

Without full chromosome attachment, stop signal is received.

@bottom-right

With full chromosome attachment, go-ahead signal is received.

