=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

Which of the following statements about mitosis is [FALSE]{color=red}?

- A) Mitosis is cell division that produces two daughter cells.
- B) Each daughter cell formed by mitosis has the half the number of chromosomes as the parent cell.
- C) Each daughter cell formed by mitosis has the same kinds of chromosomes as the parent cell.
- D) The parent cell and the daughter cells are genetically identical.

@answer

[Answer\: B]{color=red}


=== layout: two-panels

# Mitosis has four stages

@left

![Slide image 11](assets/lect06b-intro_cells/image_011.jpg)

@right

- Chromosome number does not change
- Two daughter cells are produced in the end


=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

Which of the following is the correct sequence of mitotic phases?

- A)	metaphase, anaphase, telophase, prophase
- B)	anaphase, prophase, metaphase, telophase
- C)	prophase, anaphase, metaphase, telophase
- D)	prophase, metaphase, anaphase, telophase
- E)	prophase, metaphase, telophase, anaphase

@answer

[Answer\: D, PMAT]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# Stages in Cell Division

@body

- G2 of Interphase
- 5 Stages of Mitosis\:
  - Prophase
  - Prometaphase/late prophase
  - Metaphase
  - Anaphase
  - Telophase
- Cytokinesis


